\tag{fdip}
\title{Local gauge symmetry and the scalar mean}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{A [scalar marginal weight](fdip-010E) sums over every link
assignment while holding the field fixed. At a single vertex a gauge
change can move the scalar to any other point of its orbit. What
information survives this change in the field mean or in the mean of
an individual link?}

